@page "/singularity-bot"

<PageTitle>SingularityBot // The Singularity Workshop</PageTitle>

<main class="bot-showcase">
    <header class="bot-hero">
        <a class="bot-back" href="/">✳ THE SINGULARITY WORKSHOP</a>
        <p class="bot-kicker">A WORKSHOP CREATION / STARCRAFT II</p>
        <h1>Meet <span>SingularityBot</span>.</h1>
        <p class="bot-lede">Not a script that blindly follows a build order. A decision-and-action runtime that observes a changing world, coordinates intent, and turns validated decisions into StarCraft II actions.</p>
        <div class="bot-hero-actions">
            <a class="bot-action primary" href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.SingularityBot">EXPLORE THE SOURCE ↗</a>
            <a class="bot-action" href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.SingularityBot/tree/development/docs/forge">ENTER FORGE ↗</a>
            <a class="bot-action" href="/match-viewer">MATCH VIEWER / PREVIEW ↗</a>
        </div>
        <div class="bot-statusline"><span class="status-pulse"></span> SOURCE-LED SHOWCASE <span>·</span> NO FABRICATED MATCH TELEMETRY</div>
    </header>

    <section class="bot-stage" aria-label="SingularityBot decision pipeline">
        <div class="stage-heading"><span>THE DECISION ENGINE</span><span>FOLLOW THE SIGNAL ↓</span></div>
        <div class="decision-flow">
            <article class="decision-node">
                <span class="node-number">01</span><span class="node-icon">◉</span>
                <h2>Observe</h2><p>Receive the SC2 observation and normalize visible units, resources, orders, map facts and game-loop state.</p>
                <small>SC2 PROTOCOL / NORMALIZED OBSERVATION</small>
            </article>
            <div class="flow-link" aria-hidden="true"><span>›</span></div>
            <article class="decision-node">
                <span class="node-number">02</span><span class="node-icon">◎</span>
                <h2>Understand</h2><p>Maintain match context, spatial intelligence, entity history and the current strategic picture.</p>
                <small>WORLD MODEL / PERSISTENT CONTEXT</small>
            </article>
            <div class="flow-link" aria-hidden="true"><span>›</span></div>
            <article class="decision-node">
                <span class="node-number">03</span><span class="node-icon">⌘</span>
                <h2>Coordinate</h2><p>Advisors and controllers propose strategic jobs and intents; the executive reviews and arbitrates competing work.</p>
                <small>CHIEF / COMMANDERS / STRATEGIC REVIEW</small>
            </article>
            <div class="flow-link" aria-hidden="true"><span>›</span></div>
            <article class="decision-node">
                <span class="node-number">04</span><span class="node-icon">⌁</span>
                <h2>Execute</h2><p>Unit behavior FSMs update, intents are validated against current facts, and the SC2 adapter submits legal actions.</p>
                <small>FSM_API / VALIDATION / ACTION PIPELINE</small>
            </article>
        </div>
        <p class="flow-footnote">This is a source-derived explanation of the implemented control path—not a live match feed or a simulation running in this page.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="bot-layers">
        <div class="section-intro"><span>UNDER THE HOOD</span><h2>One bot. Several cooperating systems.</h2><p>Open a layer to see what it contributes and where the responsibility lives.</p></div>
        <details open>
            <summary><span>01</span><strong>FSM_API</strong><em>Persistent behavior</em></summary>
            <p>Provides finite-state-machine execution and persistent entity contexts. Individual units can carry behavior over time instead of being treated as disposable rows in a script.</p>
            <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/FSM_API">Inspect FSM_API ↗</a>
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary><span>02</span><strong>FSM_COS</strong><em>Capability composition</em></summary>
            <p>Composes startup dependencies and runtime configuration. It is not a second game loop and does not take over the bot's live action lifecycle.</p>
            <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.FSM_COS">Inspect FSM_COS ↗</a>
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary><span>03</span><strong>Physics</strong><em>Spatial reasoning</em></summary>
            <p>Supplies spatial and path reasoning capabilities used by the bot's world model and movement decisions.</p>
            <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Physics">Inspect Physics ↗</a>
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary><span>04</span><strong>CommandAi</strong><em>Command vocabulary</em></summary>
            <p>Provides the bot-owned command vocabulary and validation boundary. It does not bypass the bot's action arbitration or submit protocol actions itself.</p>
            <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.CommandAi">Inspect CommandAi ↗</a>
        </details>
    </section>

    <section class="bot-capabilities">
        <div class="section-intro"><span>WHAT EXISTS TODAY</span><h2>Show the real work.</h2><p>These are implementation boundaries, not marketing checkmarks.</p></div>
        <div class="capability-grid">
            <article><b>Terran Marine baseline</b><p>The default match configuration is Terran, preserving the established Marine-oriented baseline. Full opening success still requires live match and replay evidence.</p><span class="capability-state implemented">IMPLEMENTED / LIVE MATCH PROOF PENDING</span></article>
            <article><b>Race-aware definitions</b><p>BotDefinition and race/mode selection provide a bounded authoring surface. A selectable opener is not the same as a complete, ladder-ready race composition.</p><span class="capability-state bounded">BOUNDED / EXPERIMENTAL</span></article>
            <article><b>Bot Studio evidence</b><p>The runtime publishes read-only snapshots and a bounded event journal. The optional bridge is loopback-only and token-protected; it is not a public browser telemetry endpoint.</p><span class="capability-state local">LOCAL INSPECTION FOUNDATION</span></article>
            <article><b>Forge editor</b><p>Author BotDefinition data, inspect JSON, run browser-side contract checks, and import or export portable definitions. Runtime validation remains authoritative.</p><span class="capability-state implemented">BROWSER AUTHORING AVAILABLE</span></article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bot-journey">
        <div><span class="section-eyebrow">THE VISITOR JOURNEY</span><h2>Understand it. Then play it. Then build your own.</h2><p>The intended experience grows in deliberate stages. We will not light up a Play button until a hosted match can actually be started, watched, stopped, adjudicated and cleaned up.</p></div>
        <div class="journey-steps">
            <article><span>01 / NOW</span><h3>Discover</h3><p>Explore the bot, its decision pipeline, source, and current evidence.</p><a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.SingularityBot/tree/development/docs">READ THE DOCUMENTATION ↗</a></article>
            <article><span>02 / NEXT</span><h3>Play</h3><p>A hosted SC2 client fills the available stage. The browser receives its video and later sends session-authorized input. No console window in the visitor view.</p><small>WAITING FOR SERVERSC2 HOST + MEDIA + CONTROL PROOF</small></article>
            <article><span>03 / GROWING</span><h3>Build</h3><p>Forge already authors portable bot definitions. The future editor-to-ladder workflow will submit immutable definitions and builds to a trusted host.</p><a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.SingularityBot/tree/development/docs/forge">OPEN FORGE SOURCE ↗</a></article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bot-match-plan">
        <div><span class="section-eyebrow">THE MATCH EXPERIENCE</span><h2>From Play to a story worth replaying.</h2><p>Our target is a complete session, not just an embedded video. The game view should occupy the available panel; after authoritative completion, the host supplies a report, replay and evidence. Then the visitor can play again or follow another experience.</p></div>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Full-stage game view</strong><span>Host-rendered SC2 video, fitted to the available panel, with the host console kept out of the visitor UI.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Authoritative match report</strong><span>Result, participants, bot build identities, map, duration, key events and evidence provenance.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Replay and moment snapshots</strong><span>Replays plus selected, spoiler-conscious screenshots that help visitors and casters judge a match's potential.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Play again or discover</strong><span>Return to the queue or move to the next Workshop experience by choice.</span></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="match-boundary">CURRENT LIMIT: ServerSC2's independent observer topology, browser media delivery, remote input, authoritative completion and replay capture are not yet proven end to end. The Play experience remains a planned integration, not an enabled service.</p>
    </section>

    <footer class="bot-footer"><a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.SingularityBot">SINGULARITYBOT SOURCE ↗</a><span>DECISIONS SHOULD BE INSPECTABLE. CLAIMS SHOULD BE PROVABLE.</span></footer>
</main>

<style>
